<title>UK: Pearson plays down satellite float report.</title>
<headline>Pearson plays down satellite float report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pearson Plc on Wednesday played down a newspaper report that the flotation of Luxembourg-based Societe Europeenne des Satellites was back on track and the company would reap a hefty cash windfall from the float.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a long-awaited event, it will happen at some time but we are not particularly awaiting it in the near future,&quot; said a spokeswoman for the company.</p>
<p>Pearson shares were down 3-1/2p at 771-1/2 by 1228 GMT after rising as much as 5p in early trading.</p>
<p>The report in the British newspaper The Independent said Pearson's six percent stake in the satellite venture could be valued at up to 180 million stg -- pushing Pearson's estimated break-up value towards 10.00 stg.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
